IMPORT prelude

-- Medicines (Advertisement and Sale) Act 1955 (Singapore) -- the ban on advertising remedies for the Schedule diseases and
-- conditions (s 3 and the Schedule), the ban on advertising for procuring miscarriage (s 5), the offences, presumption and defences
-- for both (s 6), the Minister's exemption from s 5 (s 9), and the duty to label a retail medicine with its composition in English
-- (s 7), with the definition of "substance recommended as a medicine" (s 2).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MASA1955.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021; the latest
-- amendment annotated in it is Act 11 of 2023 with effect from 26 June 2023 (s 4 repealed, s 6(1) and (3) amended, s 6(4) deleted,
-- s 9 substituted). The retrieval record says "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026".
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. It is REQ-0024 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (9 sections and one Schedule), so this row covers almost all of it. Not encoded: s 1 (short
-- title), s 3(3) (the Minister's power to amend the Schedule, beyond reading the Schedule as deposited), s 8 (District and
-- Magistrate's Court jurisdiction), and the meaning of "appropriate designation" in s 7(2)(a), which turns on the Poisons Act 1938,
-- the Poisons Rules and the British Pharmacopoeia -- here the label simply either gives a designation or it does not.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions (the skill itself was not loadable in this
-- session; the example rows were followed). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for
-- public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medicines (Advertisement and Sale) Act 1955`

§§ `Schedule -- diseases and conditions`

-- THE SCHEDULE (Sections 3 and 6(2)) DISEASES AND CONDITIONS: 1. Blindness 2. Cancer 3. Cataract 4. Drug addiction 5. Deafness
-- 6. Diabetes 7. Epilepsy or fits 8. Hypertension 9. Insanity 10. Kidney diseases 11. Leprosy 12. Menstrual disorders
-- 13. Paralysis 14. Tuberculosis 15. Sexual function 16. Infertility 17. Impotency 18. Frigidity 19. Conception and pregnancy.
-- The last three entries of the declaration below are NOT in the Schedule; they are there to be tested against it.
DECLARE Condition IS ONE OF
    `blindness`
    `cancer`
    `cataract`
    `drug addiction`
    `deafness`
    `diabetes`
    `epilepsy or fits`
    `hypertension`
    `insanity`
    `kidney diseases`
    `leprosy`
    `menstrual disorders`
    `paralysis`
    `tuberculosis`
    `sexual function`
    `infertility`
    `impotency`
    `frigidity`
    `conception and pregnancy`
    `heart disease`
    `obesity`
    `the common cold`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A Condition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition is in the Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `heart disease` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `obesity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the common cold` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3, 5, 6 and 9 -- advertisements`

-- s 2: "advertisement" includes any notice, circular, pamphlet, label, wrapper or other document, any announcement made orally or by
-- any means of producing or transmitting light or sound "and any other form of advertising".
--
-- s 3(1): "no person shall take part in the publication of any advertisement referring to any article ... in terms which are
-- calculated to lead to the use of that article ... as a medicine, appliance or remedy for the purpose of treatment of human beings
-- for any of the diseases and conditions set out in the Schedule". Proviso: it does not apply to an advertisement "published by
-- the Government or any public authority, or by the governing body of a public hospital or by any person authorised to publish the
-- advertisement by the Minister".
-- s 5: no person shall take part in publishing an advertisement referring to "any skill or service, or to any article" in terms
-- calculated to induce a person to seek advice, or to lead to the use of the article, "for procuring miscarriage of women".
--
-- The words of s 3 are "treatment of human beings". An advertisement for prevention only, or for treating animals, is outside
-- them (an inference from the words; the Act says nothing more about prevention).
DECLARE Purpose IS ONE OF
    `treating a human being`
    `preventing the condition in a human being`
    `treating an animal`
    `procuring a miscarriage`

-- s 3(2): defence to prove the advertisement was published "only so far as was reasonably necessary to bring it to the notice of"
-- members of a local or public authority or of a public hospital's governing body, registered medical practitioners, dentists,
-- nurses and midwives, pharmacists and poisons licensees, and persons training for those registers. (s 3 only.)
-- s 6(3): defence (s 3 or s 5) to prove (a) "he did not know and had no reason to believe that he was taking part in the
-- publication", or (b) publication "only in a publication of a technical character intended for circulation mainly amongst"
-- registered medical practitioners, dentists, nurses and midwives, pharmacists and poisons licensees, and trainees.
-- s 9: "The Minister may by order exempt any advertisement or class of advertisements from section 5." (Substituted by Act 11 of
-- 2023; it names s 5 only.)
DECLARE Advertisement HAS
    `published by the Government, a public authority or a public hospital's governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published by a person authorised by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published only so far as reasonably necessary to reach the listed professional classes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `published only in a technical publication for health professionals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused did not know and had no reason to believe he took part` IS A BOOLEAN
    `exempted from section 5 by the Minister's order` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the condition` IS A Condition, `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the ad` IS AN Advertisement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertisement contravenes section 3` IF
        `the condition is in the Schedule` `the condition`
    AND `the purpose` EQUALS `treating a human being`
    AND (NOT `the ad`'s `published by the Government, a public authority or a public hospital's governing body`)
    AND (NOT `the ad`'s `published by a person authorised by the Minister`)

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the ad` IS AN Advertisement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertisement contravenes section 5` IF
        `the purpose` EQUALS `procuring a miscarriage`
    AND (NOT `the ad`'s `exempted from section 5 by the Minister's order`)

GIVEN `the ad` IS AN Advertisement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 6(3) defence is proved` IF
        `the ad`'s `the accused did not know and had no reason to believe he took part`
    OR  `the ad`'s `published only in a technical publication for health professionals`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A Condition, `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the ad` IS AN Advertisement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is guilty under section 3` IF
        `the advertisement contravenes section 3` `the condition` `the purpose` `the ad`
    AND (NOT `the ad`'s `published only so far as reasonably necessary to reach the listed professional classes`)
    AND (NOT `a section 6(3) defence is proved` `the ad`)

GIVEN `the purpose` IS A Purpose, `the ad` IS AN Advertisement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is guilty under section 5` IF
        `the advertisement contravenes section 5` `the purpose` `the ad`
    AND (NOT `a section 6(3) defence is proved` `the ad`)

-- s 6(2): where it is proved that an advertisement referred to an article in the forbidden terms AND "also referred to the article
-- ... in terms calculated to indicate that it or they were manufactured, produced, imported, sold or offered for sale by the
-- person charged", then "unless the contrary is proved, it shall be presumed ... that that person took part in the publication".
GIVEN `the ad was in the forbidden terms` IS A BOOLEAN, `the ad named the accused as maker, importer or seller` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is presumed to have taken part` IF
        `the ad was in the forbidden terms`
    AND `the ad named the accused as maker, importer or seller`
    AND (NOT `the accused proved the contrary`)

§§ `6(1) and 7(3) -- penalties`

-- s 6(1) (as amended by Act 11 of 2023), contravening s 3 or 5: (a) first conviction, fine not exceeding $1,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding one year or both; (b) subsequent conviction, fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both.
-- s 7(3), selling or supplying in contravention of s 7(1) and (2): (a) first conviction, fine not exceeding $1,000 (no
-- imprisonment); (b) subsequent conviction, fine not exceeding $2,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 6 months or both.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `an advertising offence under section 3 or 5`
    `a labelling offence under section 7`

DECLARE Conviction IS ONE OF
    `a first conviction`
    `a subsequent conviction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the conviction` IS A Conviction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    IF `the conviction` EQUALS `a first conviction` THEN 1000 ELSE 2000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the conviction` IS A Conviction
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `an advertising offence under section 3 or 5`
    THEN IF `the conviction` EQUALS `a first conviction` THEN 12 ELSE 24
    ELSE IF `the conviction` EQUALS `a first conviction` THEN 0 ELSE 6

§§ `2 and 7 -- disclosing the composition of a medicine`

-- s 2: a "substance recommended as a medicine" is one referred to (a) on the article, its wrapper, container, label or an enclosed
-- document; (b) "in any placard or other document exhibited at the place where the article is sold"; or (c) in an advertisement by
-- or for the manufacturer, the seller's business or the proprietor of its brand -- "in terms which are calculated to lead to the use
-- of the substance for the prevention or treatment of any ailment, infirmity or injury affecting the human body, not being terms
-- which give a definite indication that the substance is intended to be used as, or as part of, a food or drink".
GIVEN `referred to on the article, at the place of sale, or in the maker's or seller's advertising` IS A BOOLEAN, `in terms calculated to lead to use to prevent or treat a human ailment` IS A BOOLEAN, `in terms definitely indicating a food or drink` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substance is recommended as a medicine` IF
        `referred to on the article, at the place of sale, or in the maker's or seller's advertising`
    AND `in terms calculated to lead to use to prevent or treat a human ailment`
    AND (NOT `in terms definitely indicating a food or drink`)

-- s 7(1): no person shall (a) "sell by retail" an article consisting of or comprising a substance recommended as a medicine, or
-- (b) "supply any such article as a sample for the purpose of inducing persons to buy by retail", unless there is written "in the
-- English language (as well as in any other language that may be used in addition ...) so as to be clearly legible" on the article,
-- its container (the inner container if more than one) or a label -- (c) the appropriate designation of the substance, "or of each
-- of the active constituents thereof, or of each of the ingredients"; and (d) where each constituent or ingredient is designated,
-- "the appropriate quantitative particulars". Proviso: not "any article made up and supplied for the use of a particular person,
-- being an article prescribed by reference to the needs of that person".
-- s 7(4): defence for a person charged with SELLING to prove "the sale was effected at a shop" and the article consisted wholly of
-- (a) a substance produced by "drying, crushing or comminuting (but not subjecting to any other process)" a plant, or mixtures of
-- such substances, with or without water; or (b) "a natural mineral water, or an artificial imitation thereof".
--
-- Selling other than by retail is outside s 7(1)(a) (an inference from the words "by retail").
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF
    `sold by retail`
    `supplied as a free sample to induce retail sales`
    `sold wholesale`

DECLARE Designation IS ONE OF
    `no designation`
    `the substance as a whole`
    `each active constituent`
    `each ingredient`

DECLARE Contents IS ONE OF
    `only dried, crushed or ground plants, with or without water`
    `a plant extract`
    `natural mineral water or an imitation of it`
    `a manufactured preparation`

DECLARE Supply HAS
    `mode` IS A Mode
    `recommended as a medicine` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made up and prescribed for a particular person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `written in English and clearly legible` IS A BOOLEAN
    `designation` IS A Designation
    `quantitative particulars given` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at a shop` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contents` IS A Contents

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 7 applies to the supply` IF
        `the supply`'s `recommended as a medicine`
    AND (NOT `the supply`'s `made up and prescribed for a particular person`)
    AND (    `the supply`'s `mode` EQUALS `sold by retail`
         OR  `the supply`'s `mode` EQUALS `supplied as a free sample to induce retail sales`)

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the label satisfies section 7` IF
        `the supply`'s `written in English and clearly legible`
    AND (    `the supply`'s `designation` EQUALS `the substance as a whole`
         OR  (    (    `the supply`'s `designation` EQUALS `each active constituent`
                   OR  `the supply`'s `designation` EQUALS `each ingredient`)
              AND `the supply`'s `quantitative particulars given`))

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supply contravenes section 7` IF
        `section 7 applies to the supply` `the supply`
    AND (NOT `the label satisfies section 7` `the supply`)

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 7(4) defence is available` IF
        `the supply`'s `mode` EQUALS `sold by retail`
    AND `the supply`'s `at a shop`
    AND (    `the supply`'s `contents` EQUALS `only dried, crushed or ground plants, with or without water`
         OR  `the supply`'s `contents` EQUALS `natural mineral water or an imitation of it`)

GIVEN `the supply` IS A Supply
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seller or supplier is guilty under section 7` IF
        `the supply contravenes section 7` `the supply`
    AND (NOT `the section 7(4) defence is available` `the supply`)
